{
  "title": "100: al-Aadeyaat العاديات",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nوَالْعٰدِيٰتِ ضَبْحًا ۙ‏(1)\nWAL-A’ADEYAATE ZABHAN.\nBy the snorting chargers!\nفَالْمُوْرِيٰتِ قَدْحًا ۙ‏(2)\nFAL-MOORE-YAATE QADHAN.\nAnd those that dash off (their hoofs) striking fire\nفَالْمُغِيْرٰتِ صُبْحًا ۙ‏(3)\nFAL-MOGHEERAATE SUBHAN.\nAnd those that scour to the attack at morn!\nفَاَثَرْنَ بِهٖ نَقْعًا ۙ‏(4)\nFA-ASARNA BEHI NAQ-A’N.\nAnd stir thereby the dust aloft\nفَوَسَطْنَ بِهٖ جَمْعًا ۙ‏(5)\nFA-WASATNA BEHI JAM-A’N.\nAnd penetrate through (the foe) all of them\nاِنَّ الْاِنْسَانَ لِرَبِّهٖ لَكَنُوْدٌ ۚ‏(6)\nINNAL INSAANA LE-RABBEHI LA-KANOOD.\nVerily, man unto his Lord is ungrateful\nوَاِنَّهٗ عَلٰى ذٰلِكَ لَشَهِيْدٌ ۚ‏(7)\nWA INNAHU A’LAA ZAALEKA LA-SHAHEED.\nAnd verily, He is a witness unto that\nوَاِنَّهٗ لِحُبِّ الْخَيْرِ لَشَدِيْدٌ ؕ‏(8)\nWA INNAHU LE-HUBBIL KHAYRE LA-SHADEED.\nAnd verily, in the love of wealth, he is violent\nاَفَلَا يَعْلَمُ اِذَا بُعْثِرَ مَا فِى الْقُبُوْرِۙ‏(9)\nAFALAA YA’LAMO EZAA BOA’SERA MAA FIL QOBOORE.\nWhat! Knoweth he not when, what is in the graves is raised (to life)\nوَحُصِّلَ مَا فِى الصُّدُوْرِۙ‏(10)\nWA HUSSELA MAA FIS SODOORE.\nAnd shall be made manifest whatever is in the breasts (hearts)?\nاِنَّ رَبَّهُمْ بِهِمْ يَوْمَئِذٍ لَّخَبِيْرٌ‏(11)\nINNA RABBAHUM BEHIM YAWMA-EZIL LA-KHABEER.\nVerily, their Lord, that day concerning them, will be fully aware!",
  "merits": "There are 11 verses in this Surah and it was revealed in Makkah. In a tradition from the Holy Prophet (S) it is said that the reward for reciting this Surah is equivalent to ten times the number who are present in ‘Arafah and Muzdalifa at the time of Hajj.\nImam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that those people who recite Surah al-‘Aadiyaat everyday will be counted from the companions of Ameerul Mu’mineen (a.s.) and it has also been narrated that reciting this Surah daily carries the reward of reciting the entire Qur’an. If a person has many creditors, recitation of this Surah will help clear his debts.\nIf recited by a person in fear, this Surah brings him to safety; if recited by a hungry person, it helps in his finding sustenance; if recited by a thirsty person, his thirst will be quenched."
